1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,960
Hi, we are team [Team name].

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:05,040
Our challenge: find places on Earth that resemble permanent base sites on the Moon and Mars.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:09,530
Lava Pit Atlas: the first base could be built inside a lava pit.

4
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:13,000
We map 32 lunar and martian pit candidates with NASA Trek, LROC, HiRISE and THEMIS data…

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,580
…and match each to Earth lava tubes feature by feature: what matches, and what does not.

6
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:19,510
Best Mars candidate: Elysium west flank, ~384 km from mapped ice (rough).

7
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:24,110
Next: rehearse at Earth twins, build with local ice and regolith, and launch less from Earth.

8
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:28,170
Every number is sourced. No Mars cave is confirmed — yet.
